<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 25 June <span class="n">7</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/shengzong-of-liao"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Emperor Shengzong of Liao</span><span class="tp">971–1031</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/simon-de-montfort-5th-earl-of-leicester"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/simon-de-montfort-5th-earl-of-leicester.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Simon de Montfort, 5th Earl of Leicester</span><span class="tp">c. 1175–1218</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/dorothea-of-montau"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/dorothea-of-montau.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Dorothea of Montau</span><span class="tp">1347–1394</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/jean-baptiste-du-casse"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/jean-baptiste-du-casse.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Jean-Baptiste du Casse</span><span class="tp">1646–1715</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/georg-philipp-telemann"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/georg-philipp-telemann.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Georg Philipp Telemann</span><span class="tp">1681–1767</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/george-armstrong-custer"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/george-armstrong-custer.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">George Armstrong Custer</span><span class="tp">1839–1876</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/denes-berinkey"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/denes-berinkey.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Dénes Berinkey</span><span class="tp">1871–1944</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
